IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched2-tribunal`

-- g9-tests-sched2.l4: tests of Schedule 2 (g9-sched2-tribunal.l4). Expected values were decided from the text of the Law and the calendar before the module was run.
-- Schedule 2 has its own figures (one month's notice of resignation, absence longer than 8 weeks) and is tested on them, never on Schedule 1's.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT: each regulative rule is run with #TRACE, and the outcome it must have is written in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above the trace (FULFILLED, BREACH, or STANDING).

`A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`

-- A builder for the appointment records, in the order of the fields: day of the appointment, first day of the term, day the term expires, suitable, experienced, views sought on, notice presented on,
-- serving on the day of the appointment, followed by a re-appointment, day became a member of the States, service before.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
      suitable IS A BOOLEAN
      experienced IS A BOOLEAN
      views IS A MAYBE DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE DATE
      serving IS A BOOLEAN
      followed IS A BOOLEAN
      member IS A MAYBE DATE
      service IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
GIVETH AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
`build a member appointment` day first expires suitable experienced views notice serving followed member service MEANS
    `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` OF day, first, expires, suitable, experienced, views, notice, serving, followed, member, service

GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
`no earlier service` MEANS EMPTY

`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2036 3 1), FALSE
`ten years of service` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01`

-- the appointment of 15 March 2026 for a term from 15 March 2026 to 15 March 2032 (6 years), views sought and notice presented in good time
`the member appointment of 2026` MEANS `build a member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`

§ `Schedule 2 paragraph 1: appointment`

§§ `The heading of Schedule 2`
#CHECK `Sch 2 the heading Charity Commission tribunal (inert)`

§§ `1(1): at least 4 and no more than 8 members`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least this many members of the tribunal` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint no more than this many members of the tribunal` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 3
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 4
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 6
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 9
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 0
`a member appointment, suitable and experienced` MEANS `build a member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`a member appointment, suitable but not experienced` MEANS `build a member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
`a member appointment, experienced but not suitable` MEANS `build a member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2032 3 15) FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING `no earlier service`
-- with 3 members the duty to appoint stands: an appointment of a person who appears suitable and experienced discharges it; one who lacks either does not
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` 3 `a member appointment, suitable and experienced` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` 3 `a member appointment, suitable but not experienced` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` 3 `a member appointment, experienced but not suitable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` 3 `a member appointment, suitable and experienced` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- with 4 members the duty is met
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint at least 4 persons appearing to be suitable and to have appropriate experience as members of the tribunal` 4 `a member appointment, suitable and experienced` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- the limit of 8: a ninth appointment is a breach; with 7 members an appointment is no breach and the prohibition stays in place
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must not appoint more than 8 members of the tribunal` 8 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must not appoint more than 8 members of the tribunal` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 5

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must not appoint more than 8 members of the tribunal` 8 AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

