§§ `1(7): the chair and the vice-chair`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the members Ann, Ben and Cat` MEANS LIST "Ann", "Ben", "Cat"
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Ben")
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Cat") (JUST "Ann")
-- the same person cannot be both: "one as the chair and another as the vice-chair"
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Ann")
-- each must be among the members
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Dee") (JUST "Ben")
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Dee")
-- both are needed
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Ann") NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` NOTHING (JUST "Ben")
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` NOTHING NOTHING
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(7) the Minister must designate one member as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` NOTHING NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister designates the chair and the vice-chair` AT 4

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(7) the Minister must designate one member as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` NOTHING NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(7) the Minister must designate one member as the chair and another as the vice-chair` `the members Ann, Ben and Cat` (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Ben") AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

§§ `1(8): service is honorary unless the Minister determines otherwise`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined nothing about remuneration` TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined nothing about remuneration` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States` TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that all the members are to be remunerated by the States` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that all the members are to be remunerated by the States` FALSE
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(8) the Minister may determine that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States` AT 0 WITH
