-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(8) the Minister may determine that the chair is, or all the members are, to be remunerated by the States` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

§ `Schedule 2 paragraph 2: termination of appointment`

GIVEN given IS A DATE
      writing IS A BOOLEAN
      effective IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal`
`build a member's notice of resignation` given writing effective MEANS
    `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal` OF given, writing, effective

GIVEN firstDay IS A MAYBE DATE
      lastDay IS A MAYBE DATE
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN
      ill IS A BOOLEAN
      unfit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
`build a member's grounds` firstDay lastDay absent bankrupt ill unfit MEANS
    `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` OF firstDay, lastDay, absent, bankrupt, ill, unfit

§§ `2(1)(a): resigning by giving not less than one month's notice in writing to the Minister`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the notice of resignation must be for not less than this many months` EQUALS 1
`B of F9.3` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as B`
`C of F9.3` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C`
-- one month from 31 January 2026: clamped, 28 February; rolled, 3 March
`a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` MEANS `build a member's notice of resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 2 28)
`a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 3 March 2026` MEANS `build a member's notice of resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 3)
`a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 27 February 2026` MEANS `build a member's notice of resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 2 27)
`a member's oral notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` MEANS `build a member's notice of resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) FALSE (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `A` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `B of F9.3` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `C of F9.3` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `C of F9.3` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 3 March 2026` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 3)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `A` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 27 February 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `A` `a member's oral notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) a member may resign from office by giving not less than one month's notice in writing to the Minister` `A` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 28 February 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a member of the tribunal under Schedule 2` DOES `Sch 2: a member resigns by notice in writing` AT 1

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) a member may resign from office by giving not less than one month's notice in writing to the Minister` `A` `a member's notice given on 31 January 2026 to take effect on 27 February 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a member of the tribunal under Schedule 2` DOES `Sch 2: a member resigns by notice in writing` AT 1

#CHECK `Sch 2 para 2(1) a person ceases to be a member of the tribunal in these three cases (chapeau, inert)`
#CHECK `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister may terminate the appointment after satisfying himself or herself on one of four grounds (chapeau, inert)`
#CHECK `Sch 2 para 2(4) a person's appointment as a member of the tribunal expires in these three cases (chapeau, inert)`

§§ `2(2): the Minister may terminate on one of four grounds`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the absence must be for a period longer than this many consecutive weeks` EQUALS 8
`B of F9.4` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.4 is read as B`
-- 8 weeks is 56 days. 1 March to 25 April 2026 is 56 days counted (55 elapsed); to 26 April 57 (56 elapsed); to 27 April 58 (57 elapsed).
`member absent 1 March to 25 April 2026, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 25)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`member absent 1 March to 26 April 2026, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 26)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`member absent 1 March to 27 April 2026, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 27)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`member absent 1 March to 26 April 2026, the Minister not satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 26)) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 5 weeks (35 days): a ground for the Commissioner (longer than 4 weeks) but not for a member (longer than 8 weeks)
`member absent 1 March to 4 April 2026, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 4)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`member with no ground at all` MEANS `build a member's grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`member bankrupt, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`member ill, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`member unfit, the Minister satisfied` MEANS `build a member's grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `A` `member absent 1 March to 25 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `A` `member absent 1 March to 26 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` `member absent 1 March to 26 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` `member absent 1 March to 27 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `A` `member absent 1 March to 27 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `A` `member absent 1 March to 26 April 2026, the Minister not satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `A` `member absent 1 March to 4 April 2026, the Minister satisfied`
