#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3(2) the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the matter` `the administration of the tribunal`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 3(2) the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the matter` `a determination by the tribunal`
-- who is the responsible officer: the Law says "at least one member of staff to serve as the responsible officer" and then speaks of "the responsible officer" in the singular (F9.18)
`B of F9.18` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.18 is read as B`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`no staff available` MEANS EMPTY
`staff Dee` MEANS LIST "Dee"
`staff Dee and Eli` MEANS LIST "Dee", "Eli"
