§ `Schedule 2 paragraph 4: procedure of tribunal`

§§ `4(1): who presides over a sitting`
`B of F9.15` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.15 is read as B`
-- from the text of 4(1): (a) the chair; (b) the vice-chair, if the chair is absent; (c) if both are absent, a member appointed by those present
-- reading A of F9.15 (taken): a vacant office counts as absent. (chair, vice-chair) -> who presides, from 4(1)(a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `at the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `at the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `at the sitting` `the office is vacant` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `absent from the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the vice-chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `absent from the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `absent from the sitting` `the office is vacant` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `the office is vacant` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the vice-chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `the office is vacant` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `the office is vacant` `the office is vacant` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`

-- reading B of F9.15: a vacant office is not covered by paragraph 4(1), so any case that turns on a vacant office is a refusal;
-- the chair at the sitting presides whatever the state of the vice-chair's office (4(1)(a) does not look at it)
-- (chair, vice-chair) -> who presides
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `at the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `at the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `at the sitting` `the office is vacant` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `absent from the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the vice-chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `absent from the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `absent from the sitting` `the office is vacant`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `the office is vacant` `at the sitting`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `the office is vacant` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `B of F9.15` `the office is vacant` `the office is vacant`

-- the limbs one by one (reading A): (a) when the chair is at the sitting, (b) when the chair is absent and the vice-chair is at it, (c) when both are absent
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(a) the chair presides` `A` `at the sitting`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(a) the chair presides` `A` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(b) the vice-chair presides, the chair being absent` `A` `absent from the sitting` `at the sitting`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(b) the vice-chair presides, the chair being absent` `A` `at the sitting` `at the sitting`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(b) the vice-chair presides, the chair being absent` `A` `absent from the sitting` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(c) a member appointed by the members present presides, both the chair and the vice-chair being absent` `A` `absent from the sitting` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(c) a member appointed by the members present presides, both the chair and the vice-chair being absent` `A` `the office is vacant` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(c) a member appointed by the members present presides, both the chair and the vice-chair being absent` `A` `at the sitting` `absent from the sitting`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(1)(c) a member appointed by the members present presides, both the chair and the vice-chair being absent` `A` `absent from the sitting` `at the sitting`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1)(a) the chair presides` `B of F9.15` `the office is vacant`

