§§ `4(3)(f): costs, and offences in relation to the tribunal, with a penalty not exceeding imprisonment for 2 years and a fine`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty may not exceed imprisonment for this many months` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty may not exceed imprisonment for this many days` EQUALS 730
`B of F9.13` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.13 is read as B`
-- a penalty of 24 months and a fine of a level on the standard scale, or an unlimited fine ("a fine"): within the cap in months; 25 months is over it; a fine alone, or a fine and no fine, is within it
`24 months and a fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
`25 months and a fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 25), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
`23 months and no fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 23), `no fine is provided`
`a fine of level 3 only` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3)
`no imprisonment and no fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, `no fine is provided`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` `25 months and a fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` `23 months and no fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` `a fine of level 3 only` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` `no imprisonment and no fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- reading B (the days): 24 months from 1 March 2027 is 731 days (2028 is a leap year), over the cap of 730; from 1 March 2025 it is 730 days, within it; 23 months from 1 March 2027 is 703 days
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `B of F9.13` `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `B of F9.13` `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `B of F9.13` `23 months and no fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `B of F9.13` `a fine of level 3 only` (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `B of F9.13` `no imprisonment and no fine` (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the States may by Regulations provide for costs and create offences in relation to the tribunal with a penalty not exceeding imprisonment for 2 years and a fine` `A` `24 months and a fine` (YMD 2027 3 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the States` DOES `Sch 2: the States make Regulations creating an offence in relation to the tribunal` AT 8

-- Regulations that attach a penalty above the cap are not within the power: the States' permission stays open and nothing was done under it
