§ `The readings of F9.13, F9.15 and F9.18 called directly`
-- F9.13: 24 months is within the cap in months; 25 is not
#ASSERT `F9.13 reading A: the term is within the cap when its months are at most 24` 24
#ASSERT NOT `F9.13 reading A: the term is within the cap when its months are at most 24` 25
-- F9.13: in days: 24 months from 1 March 2027 is 731 days (over 730); from 1 March 2025 it is 730 (within); 23 months from 1 March 2027 is 703 (within)
#ASSERT NOT `F9.13 reading B: the term is within the cap when its days are at most 730` 24 (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT `F9.13 reading B: the term is within the cap when its days are at most 730` 24 (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT `F9.13 reading B: the term is within the cap when its days are at most 730` 23 (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- F9.15: a vacant office
